  "result": "Fixed. The quote command now prints 27.06, and all 6 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** `to_cents` in `shop/money.py:9` padded the fractional part with `rjust` instead of `ljust`. A one-digit fraction like the \"5\" in \"12.5\" became \"05\", so the price parsed as 12.05 instead of 12.50. The rest of the pipeline was correct: 2 \u00d7 12.05 = 24.10, plus 8.25% tax, gave the wrong 26.09.\n\n**Fix:** changed the padding to `ljust(2, \"0\")`. Verified parsing for \"12.5\", \"12.50\", \"12\", \"12.05\" and \"0.5\", which now all give the expected cent values.\n\n**Tests:** pytest is not installed in this environment, so I ran the suite with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`. All 6 tests pass. Note that none of the existing tests cover `to_cents` directly, which is why this slipped through. Adding a small test for one-digit fractions would be a cheap guard.",
